            <ArticleTitle>Chondromyxoid fibroma of the fourth metatarsal.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>211-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Chondromyxoid fibroma is a rare benign tumor that is typically found in the metaphyseal ends of long tubular bones, such as the tibia. The authors describe a case of this neoplasm occurring in the foot. Treatment included complete resection with reconstruction using an autogenous fibular bone graft. The surgical technique and the advantages of using a fibular bone graft are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
